# Build context exclusions for the backend image.
#
# The context is this directory, so Docker only consults THIS file — the one at
# the repository root no longer applies. Without it the virtualenv alone adds
# hundreds of megabytes to every build, and uploaded project workspaces would be
# baked into an image layer.

# ---- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ---- python --------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- runtime data --------------------------------------------------------
data/

# ---- not needed in the image ---------------------------------------------
# `tests/` is deliberately excluded: the image runs the service, and the suite
# is run in CI against the source tree, not inside the shipped container.
tests/
scripts/
*.md
